"""
train_airbus_detector_two_phase.py

Airbus Ship Detection — image-level detector (ship-present vs ship-absent)
Two-phase training that matches your requirements:

[Phase-1]
- Train at fixed 768 only (train/val both fixed)
- Oversample POS exposure to target POS:NEG = 4:6 (target_pos_frac=0.40) via WeightedRandomSampler
- Use F2-maximizing threshold selection on VAL (always at 768)
- Save best_model.pt and last_model.pt (plus logs/config/splits/metrics)

[Phase-2]
- Strictly reuse EXACT SAME split (splits_json from Phase-1)
- Initialize from Phase-1 checkpoint (init_ckpt)
- Train-time only multi-scale training (scale jitter ms_min..ms_max), but VAL remains fixed 768
- POS transform uses bbox-guided crop that GUARANTEES "ship is included" (explicit tuning)
- Keep same POS exposure control (target_pos_frac=0.40) for fair comparison
- Threshold selection on VAL remains F2-based, same as Phase-1

Environment:
- Recommended: export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 (then device is just "cuda")
- Works on single GPU without DDP

Expected dataset layout (data_dir):
  data_dir/
    train_v2/
    train_ship_segmentations_v2.csv

Outputs per run_dir:
  - global.log / detail.log
  - config.json
  - splits.json (Phase-1) or copied metadata (Phase-2)
  - metrics_val_best.json
  - best_model.pt / last_model.pt
  - val_probs_best.npz (y_prob/y_true at best epoch)
  - bbox_cache.json (optional cache for bbox_map/pos_set)

Notes:
- We purposely avoid any "random crop that can cut ships out" for POS in Phase-2.
- If bbox info missing (rare), POS falls back to non-crop pipeline to avoid breaking labels.
"""

